hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3980","Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Ujrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During Hudaybiyyah, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by me while I was lighting a fire under my cooking pot (the narrator is unsure about one word here), and lice were falling on my face. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: O Ka'b! Are the lice troubling you? I replied: Yes, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Shave your head and offer a sacrifice, or fast"
"3982","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and asked: O Ka'b bin Ujrah! Are the lice on your head causing you trouble? T"
"3983","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me—this was at the time of the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah—while I was lighting a fir"
"3984","I replied: Yes. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then shave it and offer a sacrifice of a goat, or fast for three days, or give three sa' of dates in charity to six needy people."
"3985","“I sat with Ka’b bin ‘Ujrah in the mosque and asked him about this Verse: ‘He must pay a compensation of either fasting (three days) or giving charity (feeding six poor persons) or offering sacrifice (one sheep).’ [2:196] Ka’b said: it was revealed concerning me. I had trouble with my head, so I was carried to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, with lice crawling on my face. He said: ‘I did not think that you were suffering as much as I see. Do you have a sheep?’ I said: ‘No.’ Then this Verse was revealed: “He must pay a Fidyah (ransom) of either fasting (three days) or giving Sadaqah (charity – feeding six poor persons) or offering sacrifice (one sheep).” [2:196] He said: ‘Fasting is three days, charity is to be given to six poor persons, giving each one half of a Sa’ of food, and the sacrifice is a sheep.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3079)"
"3986","Ka’ab bin ‘Ujrah said that the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ came upon him (during their stay) at Al Hudaibiyyah. He asked do the insects of your head (lice) annoy you? He said Yes. The Prophet ﷺ said Shave your head, then sacrifice a sheep as offering or fast three days or give three sa’s of dates to six poor people. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1856)"
"3987","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I did not think that your suffering had increased to the extent that I am now seeing. Do you have a goat? I replied: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then fast for three days, or feed six needy people, giving each needy person half a sa‘ (measure). Sayyiduna Ka’b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: So this verse was revealed specifically about me, but its ruling is general for all of you."
"3988","“Labbaik ‘an Shubrumah (Here I am (O Allah) on behalf of Shubrumah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who is Shubrumah?” He said: “A relative of mine.” He said: “Have you ever performed Hajj?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then make this for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2903)"
"3989","‘Abd Allah bin Abbas said Al Fadl bin Abbas was riding the Camel behind the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ. A woman of the tribe of Khath’am came seeking his (the Prophet’s) decision (about a problem relating to Hajj). Al Fadl began to look at her and she too began to look at him. The Apostle of Allaah ﷺ would turn the face of Fadl to the other side. She said Apostle of Allaah ﷺ Allaah’s commandment that His servants should perform Hajj has come when my father is an old man and is unable to sit firmly on a Camel. May I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said yes, That was at the Farewell Pilgrimage. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1809)"
"3990","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: What do you think, if your father had a debt and you paid it off on his behalf, would it be fulfilled? He replied: Yes. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration is evidence for the permissibility of analogy (qiyas)."
"3991","“O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man and he cannot perform Hajj or ‘Umrah, and he is not able to ride the mount (due to old age).” He said: “Perform Hajj and ‘Umrah on behalf of your father.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2906)"
"3992","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked: What do you think, if your father had a debt, would you pay it off? He replied: Yes. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"3993","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: What do you think, if that woman had a debt, would you pay it off? Allah, the Exalted, is most deserving that His dues be paid."
"3994","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes! Perform Hajj in place of your father."
"3995","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to the woman: Yes."
"3996","‘Abd Allah bin Abbas said Al Fadl bin Abbas was riding the Camel behind the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ. A woman of the tribe of Khath’am came seeking his (the Prophet’s) decision (about a problem relating to Hajj). Al Fadl began to look at her and she too began to look at him. The Apostle of Allaah ﷺ would turn the face of Fadl to the other side. She said Apostle of Allaah ﷺ Allaah’s commandment that His servants should perform Hajj has come when my father is an old man and is unable to sit firmly on a Camel. May I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said yes, That was at the Farewell Pilgrimage. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1809)"
"3997","The narrator states: So the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Yes! Perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"3998","Ibn 'Umar wanted to perform Hajj in the year when Al-Hajjaj was besieging Ibn Az-Zubair, and it was said to him: ""It seems that there will be fighting between them, and I am afraid that you will prevented from performing Hajj."" He said: ""In the messenger of Allah you have a good example. I am going to do what the Messenger of Allah did. I bear witness to you that I have resolved to perform 'Umrah."" Then he set out, and when he was in Zahir Al-Baida, he said: ""Hajj and Umrah are the same thing; I bear witness to you that I have resolved to perform Hajj with my 'Umrah."" And he brought along a Hadi (sacrificial animal) that he had bought in Qudaid. Then he set out and entered Ihram for them both. When he came to Makkah he circumambulated the House and (did sa'i) between As-Safa and Al-Marwah. Then he did not do any thing more than that, and he did not offer a sacrifice, or shave his head, or cut his hair; he remained in Ihram until the Day of Sacrifice. Then he slaughtered his Hadi and shaved his head, and he thought that he had completed the Tawaf of Hajj and 'Umrah in the first Tawaf. Ibn 'Umar said: ""That is what the Messenger of Allah did. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2746)"
"3999","That when they were present with the Messenger of Allah in Al-Madinah, he sent the Hadi, and whoever wanted to enter Ihram did so, and whoever did not want to, did not. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2792)"
"4000","That when the Prophet of Allah came to Dhul-Hulaifah he marked the Hadi on the right side of its hump, the he removed the blood and garlanded it with two shoes, then he mounted his she-camel and when it stood up with him Al-Baida, he recited the Talbiyah and entered Ihram at noon and enter Ihram for Hajj. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2782)"
"4001","That when the Prophet of Allah came to Dhul-Hulaifah he marked the Hadi on the right side of its hump, the he removed the blood and garlanded it with two shoes, then he mounted his she-camel and when it stood up with him Al-Baida, he recited the Talbiyah and entered Ihram at noon and enter Ihram for Hajj. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2782)"
"4002","The Messenger of Allah (SWAS) offered the noon prayer at Dhu al-Hulaifah. He then sent for a camel and made incision in the right side of its hump ; he then took out the blood by pressing it and tied two shoes in its neck. He then rode on his mount (camel) and reached al-Baida, he raised his voice for the talbiyah for performing Hajj. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1752)"
"4003","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) marked the sacrificial animal."
"4004","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Some people should share in one sacrifice."
"4005","Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and some affluent companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) who had brought sacrificial animals with them, did not end their Ihram. When the day of sacrifice came, the Prophet (peace be upon him) sacrificed a cow on behalf of his wives. When I became pure, I performed the Tawaf of the House and also performed Sa'i (between Safa and Marwah). Then I returned to Mina and presented myself before the Prophet (peace be upon him). When we were about to depart (towards Madinah), the Prophet (peace be upon him) sent me from ""Muhassab"" with my brother Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Seat your sister behind you and let her perform Umrah from ""Taneem."" He seated me behind him, I entered into Ihram for Umrah from ""Taneem,"" I performed the Tawaf of the House, then I returned and presented myself before the Prophet (peace be upon him), and then we departed (towards Madinah)."
"4006","We sacrificed along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Hudaybiyyah a camel for seven and a cow for seven people. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2809)"
"4007","""We were with the Mesenger of Allah on a journey, when the Day of Sacrifice came, so we shared a camel among ten men, and a cow among seven."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4392)"
"4008","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sacrificed a cow on behalf of his wives."
"4009","The Messenger of Allah (SWAS) would send the sacrificial animals as offerings (to Makkah) from Madinah. I would twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals ; thereafter he would not abstain from anything from which a pilgrim putting on Ihram abstains. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1758)"
"4010","The Prophet (peace be upon him) would send those sacrificial animals (to Makkah) while he himself stayed with us in Madinah Munawwarah. Then he (peace be upon him) would not observe the restrictions of Ihram, nor would he avoid anything from which a person in Ihram abstains."
"4011","I used to twist the garlands for the sheep of the Prophet ﷺ and he would send them (to the Kaʿba), and stay as a non-Muhrim. (Using translation from Bukhārī 1703)"
"4012","""I used to twist the garlands for the Hadi of the Messenger of Allah. Then he would not avoid anything that the Muhrim avoids."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2794)"
"4013","The Messenger of Allah (SWAS) would send the sacrificial animals as offerings (to Makkah) from Madinah. I would twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals ; thereafter he would not abstain from anything from which a pilgrim putting on Ihram abstains. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1758)"
"4014","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: Ride on it. He replied: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! This is a sacrificial animal. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: May you be ruined, ride on it."
"4015","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You people may ride the sacrificial animal appropriately, until you find another animal (for riding)."
"4016","the Messenger of Allah saw a man driving a Badanah and said: ""Ride it."" He said: ""It is Badanah."" He said: ""Ride it."" He said: ""It is a Badanah."" The fourth time he said: Ride it, woe to you!"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2800)"
"4017","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You may ride the sacrificial animal in a suitable manner until you find (another) animal for riding."
"4018","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) took one hundred camels with him for sacrifice. When he (peace be upon him) reached the place of sacrifice, he (peace be upon him) sacrificed sixty-three camels with his own blessed hand, and the remaining ones he gave to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) (so that he may slaughter them)."
"4019","The narrator says: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) slaughtered seven animals while they were standing, with his blessed hand."
"4020","It was narrated from Jabir bin ‘Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that a piece from every camel that had been slaughtered be brought and placed in a pot, then they ate from its meat and drank some of the broth. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3158)"
"4021","It was narrated from ‘Ali ؓ that The Prophet ﷺ sent his sacrificial animal with him and told him to give its meat, skin and blankets in charity. (Using translation from Aḥmad 894)"
"4022","We will pay his wages ourselves (Using translation from Aḥmad 1002)"
"4023","""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What should be done with the afflicted among the Hadi?' He said: 'Slaughter them, then dip their sandals in their blood, then leave them so that the people can eat them.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 910)"
"4024","I do)? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Sacrifice it, then dye its shoes (i.e., the shoes that are hung around its neck as a garland) in its blood and mark its side with them. Do not eat from it yourself, nor should any of your companions eat its meat."
"4025","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them). So we went, and we mentioned the matter of his sacrificial animal before Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: You have asked a knowledgeable person. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent sixteen camels with a man. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed that man regarding them. The man went, then he returned and asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! If any of these animals becomes a burden for me (i.e., is unable to go further), what should I do? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Sacrifice it, then dye its (necklace’s) sandals in its blood and mark its side with them. Do not eat its meat yourself, nor should any of your companions eat its meat."
"4026","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) were going somewhere in Madinah Munawwarah when we met Sayyiduna Uth"
"4027","Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) informed him that Sayyiduna Uthman bin Maz'un (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to remain celibate, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade him from this. Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: If the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had permitted him, we would have had ourselves castrated."
"4028","I will boast of your numbers before the Prophets on the Day of Resurrection."
"4029","The command of Allah Almighty is) ""This is more appropriate so that you do not commit 'aul'."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) says that what is meant by this is: Do not commit injustice."
"4030","""There are three, all of whom have a promise of help from Allah: 'The Mujahid who strives in the cause of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime; the man who gets married, seeking to keep himself chaste; and the slave who has a contract of manumission and wants to buy his freedom.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3120)"
"4031","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr bin Al-'As that the Messenger of Allah said: ""This world is all temporary conveniences, and the best temporary convenience of this world is a righteous woman."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3232)"
"4032","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Four things are signs of good fortune: a righteous wife, a spacious house, a good neighbor, and a good mount. And four things are signs of misfortune: a bad neighbor, a bad wife, a cramped house, and a bad mount.”"
"4033","If there is bad luck in anything, it is the horse, the abode and the woman. (Using translation from Muslim 2225f)"
"4034","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among them (wives) is the one whose dowry is the least."
"4035","The narrator states: It was the practice of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that when any of their women became widowed or divorced, they would not marry her off until they knew whether the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wished to marry her or not. One day, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to an Ansari: ""O so-and-so, marry off your daughter."" He replied: ""Yes! With pleasure."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not wish to marry her myself."" The Ansari asked: ""Then to whom should I marry her?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To Julaibib."" He replied: ""O Messenger of Allah (please allow me) so that I may consult the girl's mother."" Then the man went to the woman and informed her that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had sent a marriage proposal for their daughter. The woman said: ""Alright, with pleasure."" The man said: ""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not send the proposal for himself."" The woman asked: ""Then for whom did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) send the proposal?"" The man replied: ""For Julaibib."" The woman said: ""For that unworthy Julaibib?"" Then the woman said: ""No, by Allah! I will not marry (my daughter) to Julaibib."" When the girl's father got up to go to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), the girl said from behind the curtain to her mother: ""Who has sent the marriage proposal for me?"" Both of them replied: ""The Messenger of Allah."" The girl asked: ""Will you not act upon the command of the Messenger of Allah? Hand me over to the Messenger of Allah, he will not let me go to waste."" Then the girl's father presented himself before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""The matter of this girl is in your hands."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) married the girl to Julaibib. The narrator named Hammad says: The narrator named Ishaq bin Abdullah stated: ""Do you know what supplication the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made for this girl?"" The narrator asked: ""What supplication did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) make for her?"" Ishaq replied: ""(The Prophet made this supplication:) 'O Allah! Pour goodness upon both of them abundantly and do not let any hardship come in their life.'"" Here, the narrator named Thabit has narrated these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) married the girl to that man. Once, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went out to participate in a battle and asked: ""Do you find anyone absent?"" They replied: ""No."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""But I find Julaibib absent. So search for him among the slain."" They found Julaibib in such a state that he was among seven polytheists; he had killed those seven polytheists and then was martyred himself. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""Did he kill seven men and then was martyred himself? He is from me and I am from him."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this seven times. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) lifted him up with his own arms; his only bier was the arms of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), until the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) himself placed him in his grave. The narrator named Thabit states: There was no widow among the Ansar who was more generous in spending (i.e., wealthier) than her (the wife of Julaibib)."
"4036","A woman may be married for four reasons: for her property, her status. her beauty and her religion, so try to get one who is religious, may your hand be besmeared with dust. (Using translation from Muslim 1466)"
"4037","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A woman is married either for her wealth, or for her beauty, or for her religion, so you should choose the one with religion and good character, may your hands be dusted."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, states) The paternal aunt of the narrator Sa'id bin Ishaq refers to Zainab, the daughter of Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Ujrah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"4038","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is something in their eyes."
"4039","Hafsah bint 'Umar became the widow of Khunais or Hudhaifah bin Hudhafah - 'Abdur-Razzaq was not certain. He was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who were present at Badr, and he died in Madinah, I met 'Uthman bin ʿAffan and offered I Hafsah to him in marriage, I said: If you wish, I will marry Hafsah to you. He said: I will think about it. A few days passed, then he met me and said: I do not want to get married at present. 'Umar said: Then I met Abu Bakr and I said: If you wish, I will marry Hafsah the daughter of ‘Umar to you. He did not give any response to me, and I was more upset with him than with 'Uthman. A few days passed, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed marriage to her and he gave her in marriage to him. Abu Bakr met me and said: Perhaps you felt upset with me when you offered Hafsah to me in marriage and I did not give you any response? I said: Yes. He said: Nothing prevented me from giving you an answer when you offered her to me in marriage except that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention her and I did not want to disclose the private matters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If he had not married her, I would have married her. (Using translation from Aḥmad 74)"
"4040","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, saying: Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Haywah informed me that al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid informed him that Ayyub ibn Khalid ibn Abi Ayyub al-Ansari narrated to him from his father, from his grandfather Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hide the proposal, then perform ablution and do it well, then pray as Allah has decreed for you, then praise and glorify your Lord, then say: 'O Allah, You are able and I am not, You know and I do not, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If You see that (so-and-so) – and name her – is good for me in my religion, my worldly life, and my Hereafter, then decree her for me; and if another is better for me than her in my religion, my worldly life, and my Hereafter, then decree that for me.'"""",Would you like a translation to any other language?"
"4041","""Look at her, for there is something in the eyes of the Ansar."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3247)"
"4042","Abu Ya'la informed us, saying: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us from Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Hathmah from his uncle Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, who said: I saw Muhammad ibn Maslamah (may Allah be pleased with him) chasing the daughter of al-Dahhak on a mound of the mounds of Madinah, looking at her. I said to him: ""Do you do this while you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" He said: ""Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'When Allah casts into a man's heart a proposal for a woman, there is no harm in him looking at her.'"""
"4043","Imran ibn Musa informed us, saying: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar informed us from Thabit from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him) proposed to a woman, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""Go and look at her, for that is more likely to foster love between you."""
"4044","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, saying: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us from Yazid ibn Kaysan from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned to him his marriage to a woman from the Ansar. He said: ""Look at her, for in the eyes of the Ansar there is something."""
"4045","Ibn Khuzaymah informed us, saying: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Fatimah bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her): ""Go to Umm Sharik, and do not deprive us of yourself."""
"4046","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Zuhayr informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Asim informed us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us from Dawud ibn Farahij from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should not outbid his brother, nor propose over his brother's proposal, nor should a woman ask for the divorce of her sister to turn over what is in her bowl."" The Shaykh Ibn Zayd said: This (narrator) is from the people of Mazar, a Basran, trustworthy."
"4047","Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Sinan informed us, saying: Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr informed us from Malik from Nafi' from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should propose over the proposal of his brother."""
"4048","al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab informed us, saying: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he forbade that a man should outbid his brother or propose over his brother's proposal."
"4049","Abu Salamah bin ‘Abd Al Rahman reported on the authority of Fatimah daughter of Qais Abu ‘Amr bin Hafs divorced her (Fatimah daughter of Qais) absolutely when he was away from home and his agent sent her home barley. She was displeased with it. He said “I swear by Allah, you have no claim on us. She then came to Apostle of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said to her “No maintenance is due to you from him. He ordered her to spend the waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik but he said afterwards “that is a woman whom my Companions visit. Spend the waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum for he is blind and you can undress. Then when you are in a position of being remarried, tell me.” She said “When I was in a position to remarry, I mentioned to him that Mu’awiyah bin Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm had asked me in marriage. The Apostle of Allah ﷺsaid “As for Abu Jahm, he does not put down his stick from his shoulder, and as for Mu’awiyah he is a poor man who has no property; marry Usamah bin Zaid. I disliked him but he said “Marry Usamah bin Zaid. So, I married him. And Allah prospered him very much and I was envied.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2284)"
"4050","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No person should bid against his brother's bid until (the other person) buys it or leaves the deal, and no person should send a marriage proposal over his brother's proposal until (the other person) marries or leaves the proposal."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Kathir is Yazid bin Abdur Rahman bin Udhaynah."
"4051","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""No person should send a marriage proposal over the proposal of his brother until the first proposer leaves it or gives permission, then he may send a marriage proposal."
"4052","narrates: When someone intended to get married, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would say to him, ""May Allah grant you blessings and shower blessings upon you."
"4053","Sayyiduna Abu Burdah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me from Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash’ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When a person brings up his slave girl well and gives her a good upbringing, teaches her well and gives her a good education, then frees her and marries her, that person will have a double reward. And whoever believes in Sayyiduna ‘Isa (Jesus, peace be upon him) and then believes in me, he will also have a double reward. And the slave who fears his Lord and obeys his master, he will also have a double reward.”"
"4054","I saw her, and I did not like her, because I realized that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would also like her in the same way as I did. Juwayriya said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! The situation is as you know. I have made a contract of manumission, and now I have come to seek help from the Messenger of Allah. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Would you not prefer something better than that? The woman asked: What is that? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I will marry you and pay your contract of manumission for you. The woman said: That is fine. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then I will do so. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Muslims heard of this, they said: Now they have become the in-laws of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so all those who had captives from Banu Mustaliq freed them all. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Because of the marriage of Lady Juwayriya (may Allah be pleased with her) to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), one hundred families of Banu Mustaliq were freed. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: To my knowledge, there is no other woman who proved to be a greater blessing for her people than Lady Juwayriya."
"4055","I saw her, and I disliked her, because I realized that just as she appeared beautiful to me, she would also appear so to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). Juwayriya said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! The situation is as you know. I have made a contract of emancipation for myself, so I have come to seek help from the Messenger of Allah. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Will you not choose something better than that? She asked: What is that? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: I will marry you and pay the amount of your contract on your behalf. She said: That is fine. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Then I will do so. When the Muslims heard of this, they said: These people have become the in-laws of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), so they freed all the captives of Banu Mustaliq who were with them. Because of the Prophet Muhammad’s (peace be upon him) marriage, one hundred families of Banu Mustaliq were set free. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: To my knowledge, there is no woman who proved to be a greater blessing for her people than Lady Juwayriya (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"4056","A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have found a woman of rank and beauty, but she does not give birth to children. Should I marry her? He said: No. He came again to him, but he prohibited him. He came to him third time, and he (the Prophet) said: Marry women who are loving and very prolific, for I shall outnumber the peoples by you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2050)"
"4057","A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have found a woman of rank and beauty, but she does not give birth to children. Should I marry her? He said: No. He came again to him, but he prohibited him. He came to him third time, and he (the Prophet) said: Marry women who are loving and very prolific, for I shall outnumber the peoples by you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2050)"
"4058","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) married her in the month of Shawwal, and her departure to his house also took place in the month of Shawwal. And among the wives of the Prophet (peace be upon him), who was more beloved to him than me?"
"4059","I will consult the girl's mother. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Alright. That man went to his wife and mentioned this matter to her. The woman said: By Allah, no! This cannot happen. We had even refused proposals from so-and-so and so-and-so for this girl. The narrator says: The girl was listening to this conversation from behind a curtain. The girl said: Will you not accept the request of Allah's Messenger? If the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is pleased with this proposal, then marry me to him. Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was as if the girl made things easy for her parents. They replied: You have spoken rightly. Then her father went to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: If you are pleased with this man, then we are also pleased with him. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I am pleased with him. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) married the girl to Sayyiduna Julaibib (may Allah be pleased with him). (After some time) the people of Madinah were struck with fear (i.e., there was a battle), and the wife of Sayyiduna Julaibib (may Allah be pleased with him) also went out. She found her husband in such a state that he had been martyred, and beneath him were some slain polytheists whom Sayyiduna Julaibib (may Allah be pleased with him) had killed. Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I have not seen any widow in Madinah who spent more (in the way of Allah) than that woman."
"4060","""How much did you give her?"" He said: ""A Nawah (five Dirhams) of gold."" The Messenger of Allah said: ""Give a Walimah (wedding feast) even if it is with one sheep."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3351)"
"4061","The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyyah with meal and dates. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3744)"
"4062","I was with him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) reached the house of his new noble wife, there were two men sitting in a corner of the house, talking to each other. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw them, he turned back and left. (On this occasion) Allah Almighty revealed the verse regarding the command of hijab."
"4063","Messenger of Allah ﷺ manumitted Safiyya and then married her, and her Mahr was her manumission, and he gave a wedding banquet with Hais (a sort of sweet dish made from butter, cheese and dates). (Using translation from Bukhārī 5169)"
"4064","The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyyah with meal and dates. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3744)"
"4065",": : "" "" : "" "" "" "" . Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When she came to Madinah Munawwarah, she informed the people that she was the daughter of Umayyah bin Mughirah. The people did not accept her statement. They began to say: What a strange and astonishing falsehood this is. Then, when some of those people intended to go for Hajj, they said: Will you write a letter to your family? So I wrote a letter and gave it to those people. When they returned, they confirmed the statement of Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), and thus her honor and respect increased. Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When Zainab was born to me, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and proposed marriage to me. I said: A woman like me cannot be married, because I am no longer able to bear children, and I have a bit of a sharp temperament, and I am also a mother of children. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am older than you in age. As for the sharpness of temperament, Allah the Exalted will remove it. As for the children, they are entrusted to Allah and His Messenger. Then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will come to you tonight. Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I took out some barley grains from my pouch and some fat, and I prepared it for the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the night there. In the morning, he said: You hold an honorable position with your husband. If you wish, I will stay with you for seven days. If I stay with you for seven days, I will also stay with my other wives for seven days each."
"4066","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair, may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): \""Announce the marriage.\"" The Sheikh explains: The words of the narration \""You people announce\"" mean: (perform the offer and acceptance) in the presence of two just witnesses."""
"4067","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""O Banu Bayadah! Arrange the marriage of Abu Hind (marry a girl or woman from your family to him)."" (Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) states that he used to practice cupping.)"
"4068","One should not combine in marriage a woman with her father's sister, or her mother's sister. (Using translation from Muslim 1408e)"
"4069","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""No woman should ask for the divorce of her sister (Muslim) so as to take her place, but she should marry the man (without compelling him to divorce his other wife), for she will have nothing but what Allah has written for her."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6601)"
"4070","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""No woman should demand the divorce of her sister so that she may obtain her share of blessings herself, for a Muslim woman is the sister of another Muslim woman."
"4071","narrates: His sister was the wife of a certain man. That man divorced her and then left her as she was until her waiting period ('iddah) was over. Then that man sent a proposal for marriage again. Sayyiduna Ma'qil (may Allah be pleased with him) became angry at this and said: He left this woman like that even though he could have taken her back. Sayyiduna Ma'qil (may Allah be pleased with him) became an obstacle in this matter, so Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""And when you divorce women and they have fulfilled their waiting period, do not prevent them from marrying their (former) husbands if they agree among themselves in a suitable manner."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In this narration, it is omitted that the woman later married another man (then she was divorced by him or became a widow, and then the first husband sent a marriage proposal)."
"4072","I marry you to such-and-such woman? He said: Yes. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked the woman: Are you pleased that I marry you to such-and-such man? The woman replied: Yes. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) married her to him. He did not fix any dowry. The woman was sent to her husband's house and the man did not give her anything. When the man was near death, he said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah married me to such-and-such woman and I did not give her any dowry. I give her my share in Khaybar."
"4073",""" If you fear that you will not be able to maintain equity amongst the orphan girls, then marry (those) you like from amongst the women two, three or four."" She said: O, the son of my sister, the orphan girl is one who is under the patronage of her guardian and she shares with him in his property and her property and beauty fascinate him and her guardian makes up his mind to marry her without giving her due share of the wedding money and is not prepared (to pay so much amount) which anyone else is prepared to pay and so Allah has forbidden to marry these girls but in case when equity is observed as regards the wedding money and they are prepared to pay them the full amount of the wedding money and Allah commanded to marry other women besides them according to the liking of their heart. 'Urwa reported that 'A'isha said that people began to seek verdict from Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the revelation of this verse about them (orphan girls) and Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, revealed this verse:"" They asked thee verdict about women; say: Allah gives verdict to you in regard to them and what is recited to you in the Book about orphan woman, whom you give not what is ordained for them while you like to marry them"" (iv. 126). She said: The wording of Allah"" what is recited to you"" in the Book means the first verse, i. e."" if you fear that you may not be able to observe equity in case of an orphan woman, marry what you like in case of woman"" (iv. 3). 'A'isha said: (And as for this verse [iv. 126], i. e. and you intend"" to marry one of them from amongst the orphan girls"" it pertains to one who is in charge (of orphans) having small amount of wealth and less beauty and they have been forbidden that they should marry what they like of her wealth and beauty out of the orphan girls, but with equity, because of their disliking for them. (Using translation from Muslim 3018a)"
"4074","I met Zuhri, I mentioned this narration before him, and he was not aware of it. However, this is not something that would weaken a report of this nature. The reason is: Sometimes, a knowledgeable, virtuous, pious, and reliable person narrates a hadith, and then he forgets it, and when he is later asked about this hadith, he does not remember it. So, his forgetting something he had narrated does not indicate that the original narration is invalid. Our master Muhammad Mustafa (peace and blessings be upon him) is the best of mankind; he forgot while performing prayer. It was said in his presence: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Has the prayer been shortened, or did you forget? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Neither of the two has happened. So, the personality whom Allah Almighty chose for His Prophethood and granted infallibility among His creation, even he could be affected by forgetfulness regarding the matter most frequently practiced by Muslims, which is prayer, to the extent that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forgot, and when people asked him about it, he denied it. The Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) forgetfulness does not indicate that the ruling he forgot is invalid. (So, if this is the case,) then after the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), those people from his Ummah who are not infallible, it is even more likely for them to be affected by forgetfulness, and in the presence of forgetfulness, it is not permissible to use this as evidence that something is invalid which was authentically established from them before they forgot."
"4075","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There is no marriage without a guardian and two just witnesses; any marriage other than this will be considered invalid. And if there is a dispute among people regarding (the matter of a guardian), then whoever has no guardian, the ruler of the time is his guardian. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In the narration transmitted from Zuhri through Sulaiman bin Musa from Ibn Jurayj, the words ""without two just witnesses"" have only been narrated by three individuals: Saeed bin Yahya Umavi narrated it from Hafs bin Ghiyath; Abdullah bin Abdulwahab Hajbi narrated it from Khalid bin Harith; and Abdur Rahman bin Yunus Ruqi narrated it from Isa bin Yunus. The mention of two witnesses has not been authentically transmitted anywhere else in this narration."
"4076","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no marriage without a guardian (wali)."" The narrator named Abu Amir is Salih bin Rustam."
"4077","the Messenger of Allah said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1881)"
"4078","the Messenger of Allah said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1881)"
"4079","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'An orphan girl should be consulted with regard to marriage, and if she remains silent, that is her permission. If she refuses then she is not to be forced.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3270)"
"4080","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: In the marriage of girls, seek their consent. It was asked, ""A virgin girl feels shy."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Her silence will be her consent."
"4081","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Women should be consulted regarding their marriage. Sayyida Aisha said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon you)! A virgin girl feels shy and remains silent (so what is the ruling in this case)? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Her silence is her consent."
"4082","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Her consent is her silence."
"4083","the Messenger of Allah said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1881)"
"4084","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A previously married woman (i.e., widow or divorcee) has more right over herself than her guardian, and the consent of a virgin girl should be sought regarding herself; her silence is her permission."
"4085","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said:"
"4087","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""A widow has more right regarding herself than her guardian, and the permission of a virgin girl should be sought regarding herself, and her silence is her permission.\"" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), \""A widow has more right regarding herself,\"" means: She has more r"
"4088","Ibn ‘Abbas reported the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying “A woman without a husband has more right to her person than her guardian and a virgin’s permission must be asked, her permission being her silence. These are the words of Al Qa’nabi. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2098)"
"4089","The Prophet ﷺ said: A guardian has no concern with a woman previously married and has no husband, and an orphan girl (i.e. virgin) must be consulted, her silence being her acceptance. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2100)"
"4090","the Messenger of Allah said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1881)"
"4091","Anas bin ‘Malik said “The Prophet ﷺ manumitted Safiyyah and made her manumission her dower.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2054)"
"4092","that the Prophet said: “The conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those by means of which the private parts become permissible for you.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1954)"
"4093","A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Messenger of Allah, I have offered myself to you. When she stood for a long time, a man got up and said: Messenger of Allah, marry her to me if you have no need for her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: Have you anything to give her as dower ? He replied: I have nothing by this lower garment of mine. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If you give your lower garment, you will sit while you have no lower garment. So look for something else. He said: I do not find anything. He said: Look for something, even though it should be an iron ring. The man sought it but found nothing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do you know anything from the Qur'an ? He said: Yes, I know surah so and so, which he named. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I have given you her in marriage for the part of the Qur'an which you know. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2111)"
"4094","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: How much dowry did you give her? He replied: Four uqiyah. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Four uqiyah is as if you have searched for silver equal to the width of this mountain."
"4095","I say from myself that among the signs of a woman's misfortune is that her matters are difficult and her dowry is large."
